# Roadmap

Status icons: ⬜ not started · 🟡 in progress · ✅ done

Implementation detail lives in `.implementation/wave-N/phase-X.Y.md`. Use `/implement phase-X.Y` when a phase is tagged `[composer]` or `[opus]` only.

---

## Wave 1 — Rules engine & scaffold ✅

**Wave goal:** Runnable React app shell and a **pure, tested** Ludo rules engine with no UI dependency.

**Acceptance test:**

1. `pnpm install` and `pnpm dev` open a placeholder app.
2. `pnpm test` runs unit tests for moves, captures, sixes, three-sixes, and win detection.
3. Rules module has **zero** imports from React or Workers.

**Phases:** 1.1 ✅ · 1.2 ✅ · 1.3 ✅

---

## Wave 2 — Local playable UI ✅

**Wave goal:** Play a full local game (2–4 humans and/or CPUs) with minimal classic board UI, animations, and **30s human turn timer**.

**Acceptance test:**

1. New game setup: pick 2–4 seats, Human/CPU per seat → play through win.
2. Dice and pieces animate; classic four-color board; usable on phone width.
3. Human turn forfeits after 30s countdown; illegal moves rejected.

**Phases:** 2.1 ✅ · 2.2 ✅ · 2.3 ✅

---

## Wave 3 — CPU opponents ⬜

**Wave goal:** Any Human/CPU mix from setup (0–4 humans, including all-CPU test mode if enabled).

**Acceptance test:**

1. Examples: 1 human + 3 CPU, 4 humans, 2 human + 2 CPU — all start and finish correctly.
2. CPUs auto-play with thinking delay; humans use timer when applicable.
3. CPUs feel competitive in manual playtest.

**Phases:** 3.1 ✅ · 3.2 ✅ · 3.3 ✅

---

## Wave 4 — Online multiplayer ⬜

**Wave goal:** Live online games on Cloudflare (Pages + Worker + Durable Object per room).

**Acceptance test:**

1. `wrangler dev`: host creates room, shares code/link; second client joins.
2. Board and dice stay in sync; **30s timer** enforced for human seats online.
3. Up to 4 human joiners possible; empty CPU seats run on server when configured.

**Phases:** 4.1 ✅ · 4.2 ⬜ · 4.3 ⬜

---

## Wave 5 — PWA & production deploy ⬜

**Wave goal:** Installable PWA and production deploy via Wrangler to Cloudflare.

**Acceptance test:**

1. Lighthouse PWA checks pass (installable, manifest, SW).
2. `pnpm deploy` publishes Pages + Worker + DO bindings.
3. Production smoke: create room, join from phone, complete one timed human turn.

**Phases:** 5.1 ⬜ · 5.2 ⬜

